---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { contact, ownerSupplied } from "../data/site";

const description =
  "Delivery, service timing, cancellations and refunds for Straight Up Digital website projects, digital reports and recurring hosting services.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Delivery, cancellations and refunds"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/policies"
>
  <section class="legal">
    <div class="container legal__inner">
      <h1>Delivery, cancellations and refunds</h1>
      <p class="legal__meta">Version 1.0 · Last updated 25 November 2026</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Straight Up Digital provides digital services. We do not ship physical
          products through this website. This policy explains how project work,
          digital files, reports and hosting are delivered, and how cancellations
          and refunds are handled. It does not take away any rights provided by
          South African law. If a law gives you a stronger right, that right applies.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Business and contact details</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>{ownerSupplied.legalEntity}</strong>, trading as Straight Up
          Digital, operates from {contact.address}. Contact us at
          <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> or
          <a href={`tel:${contact.phoneInternational.replace(/[^\d+]/g, "")}`}>
            {contact.phoneInternational}
          </a>.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What is delivered and when</h2>
        <p>
          The accepted written quote or service agreement is the order record. It
          identifies the service, included work, total price, applicable taxes or
          third-party charges, payment schedule, agreed delivery date or timeframe,
          customer inputs needed, and any ongoing service period. Please review it
          and correct any errors before accepting. A website enquiry is not an
          order and does not charge you.
        </p>
        <p>
          Website designs, builds, audit reports, advice and other project outputs
          are delivered electronically, normally by email, a secure link, an online
          preview or an agreed website address. There is no shipping charge and no
          physical parcel. The quote states the delivery method and timing. Unless
          the quote says otherwise, the delivery period starts after we receive the
          agreed starting payment and the customer has supplied the information,
          content, approvals and access needed to do the work. We will tell you
          about a delay and agree a revised date.
        </p>
        <p>
          For a standalone website build, the confirmed package price is split
          50% to start and 50% at launch. We show you a preview before the launch
          balance is due. A discounted annual bundle is paid in full once-off and
          includes the agreed build plus the first year of hosting. Its recurring
          annual hosting term begins after that included year. The accepted quote
          confirms the bundle total, package, hosting plan, start date and renewal
          terms. A monthly hosting plan renews at its stated monthly rate. We will
          state the selected plan's price and renewal timing before you authorise
          payment.
        </p>
        <p>
          Hosting and email services are provisioned electronically after the order
          is accepted and the agreed payment and setup requirements are complete.
          The start date and service period are stated in the quote or order
          confirmation. Customer-owned domains, third-party booking services,
          software licences and other external services may have their own delivery
          times, fees and terms, which we will identify where applicable.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Cancelling before work starts</h2>
        <p>
          Contact us as soon as possible at
          <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> to request a
          cancellation. Include your name, business name, quote or order reference,
          and the service you want to cancel. We will confirm receipt and explain
          the next step.
        </p>
        <p>
          If work or service has not started, we will assess the amount paid and
          refund any amount due under the accepted agreement and applicable law.
          We will not charge for work that was not performed. Any permitted amount
          for work already completed, unavoidable third-party commitments or a
          reasonable cancellation charge must be supported by the agreement and
          applicable law; it will not be applied as an automatic penalty.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Cancelling after work or a recurring service starts</h2>
        <p>
          For a project already in progress, we will identify work completed,
          approved third-party costs and any remaining unperformed work. Any amount
          retained or refunded will be assessed against the accepted scope, work
          actually performed, applicable law and any cancellation rights that
          apply. We will provide an itemised explanation. If a project is cancelled
          before completion, work not performed is not automatically treated as
          earned.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may ask to cancel a monthly or annual recurring service by emailing
          <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>. We will confirm
          the effective date and whether another renewal is due. If the Consumer
          Protection Act or another law gives you a right to cancel a fixed-term
          agreement on notice, we will follow that law, including any limit on a
          reasonable cancellation charge. This policy does not create a minimum
          term that is not stated in your accepted plan or agreement.
        </p>
        <p>
          A discounted annual bundle includes its first hosting year in the
          once-off price. The later annual hosting service is a recurring service;
          the agreed renewal price and timing will be disclosed before you accept
          the bundle. You can request cancellation of future renewals. Any refund
          for a period already started is considered under the accepted agreement
          and your statutory rights; no term of this policy removes rights you
          cannot lawfully waive.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Online purchase cancellation rights</h2>
        <p>
          Where section 44 of the Electronic Communications and Transactions Act
          applies to an online transaction, a consumer may cancel a service
          transaction within seven days after concluding the agreement, without a
          reason or penalty. Where payment has already been made, the Act provides
          for a full refund within 30 days after cancellation. The Act contains
          exceptions, including where a service began with the consumer's consent
          before the end of the seven-day period. Whether an exception applies
          depends on the transaction and the facts. Any consent to begin early will
          be requested clearly; please contact us if you want to exercise a
          cancellation right.
        </p>
        <p>
          Other rights may also apply, including rights under the Consumer
          Protection Act for direct-marketing transactions, fixed-term services,
          advance bookings and unsatisfactory services. We will assess each request
          under the law that applies. Nothing here limits a consumer's rights to
          timely, quality service or an appropriate remedy where the law provides
          one.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Service problems and remedies</h2>
        <p>
          Tell us promptly if a delivered service does not match the accepted scope,
          is materially incomplete or has a fault. We will review the issue and, if
          appropriate, correct or complete the work, or provide another remedy
          required by the agreement or law. Where a service is substandard, the
          Consumer Protection Act may require the supplier to remedy the defect or
          refund a reasonable portion of the price. The facts and work performed
          will be considered in each case.
        </p>
        <p>
          A search-ranking, traffic or revenue result is not promised unless a
          written agreement expressly says otherwise. A change in a third-party
          platform, domain provider or booking service is not by itself proof that
          the agreed work was defective, but we will help identify the issue and
          explain any separately chargeable work before proceeding.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Refund processing</h2>
        <p>
          If a refund is due, we will confirm the amount and process it through the
          original payment method where available, or agree another lawful method
          with you. Refund timing may depend on the payment provider and your bank.
          Paystack states that customers generally receive a processed refund
          within 3 to 10 working days; this is the provider's estimate, not a
          guarantee by Straight Up Digital. We will share the refund reference or
          status where available. Provider processing charges paid by us do not
          reduce a refund to which you are legally entitled.
        </p>

        <h2>8. How to contact us about an order</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> with
          “Cancellation”, “Refund” or “Delivery” in the subject line, or use the
          <a href="/contact">enquiry form</a>. We aim to acknowledge your request
          within two business days. If a law sets a shorter deadline, the legal
          deadline applies.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Related terms and changes</h2>
        <p>
          Read this policy with our <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> and
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>. The accepted quote or agreement
          gives the order-specific scope and schedule. If this policy, an agreement
          and the law differ, applicable law prevails. We may update this policy;
          the version date above will change. The version supplied with your order
          remains part of your transaction record.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
